Third-party components keep their own licenses:

- three.js (MIT License), loaded from cdnjs at runtime. The isolated vehicle preview also includes unchanged r128 local copies and GLTFLoader, with the full notice at media/vehicles/vendor/THREE-LICENSE.txt.
- Map data © OpenStreetMap contributors, licensed under the Open Database
  License (ODbL) 1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/
  Any redistribution of the extracted OpenStreetMap data must follow the
  ODbL, including its attribution and share-alike terms.
- Elevation tiles: Mapzen terrarium terrain tiles on AWS Open Data.
  See the dataset's terms before reusing them.

- Kenney Car Kit 3.1 GLB review candidates in `media/vehicles/traffic/`:
  original models by Kenney, Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal,
  https://kenney.nl/assets/car-kit ; unchanged copy from the public
  https://github.com/Hidencod/tge-assets mirror on 2026-11-13.

Nissan Micra K11 authoring experiment:
- experiments/micra1995/ and media/vehicles/micra-k11.glb contain original
  procedurally authored geometry for this repository; no third-party car mesh,
  photograph, brochure scan or texture is embedded in the asset.
- Reference photographs and Nissan/JAF documentation are linked with their
  source/author/licence scope in experiments/micra1995/references.md, not bundled.
- The external Blender Modeler tooling is not vendored; its pinned source and
  reproduction instructions are documented in the experiment README.
